The Cost Impact section is good as written. Saying there is no direct budget reduction and that the value comes from recovered engineering capacity is credible and avoids overstating savings.

The Stakeholders section is also reasonable. I would consider adding the metric/business owner and downstream Splunk/reporting consumers explicitly if those roles are confirmed, because Splunk publication/reconciliation is part of the agreed automation flow.

